 61ZN    40CA(24MG,2PNG)               2006AN31                  15NDS    201503
 61ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61ZN2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61ZN c  2006An31 (also 2005An03,2005Ek01): E=104 MeV. Measured E|g, |g|g, I|g, 
 61ZN2c  |g(|q) using the CLARION Ge detector array, and the Recoil Mass        
 61ZN3c  Spectrometer (RMS). The CLARION array was comprised of ten Ge          
 61ZN4c  Clover detectors placed in a three ring configuration at 90|', 132|',  
 61ZN5c  and 154|' with respect to the beam direction.                          
 61ZN7c  Comparison of experimental and theoretical branching ratios are given  
 61ZN8c  in Table 2 of 2006An31 and levels in Fig.6. using large-scale          
 61ZN9c  shell-model calculations (code ANTOINE with GXPF1).                    
 61ZN c  2004Iz01: E=96 MeV {+40}Ca beam provided by LNL Tandem accelerator,    
 61ZN2c  bombarding a {+24}Mg target. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO),   
 61ZN3c  |g|g(lin pol) with the EUROBALL Ge-detector array consisting of 26     
 61ZN4c  Clover detectors and 15 Cluster detectors. Evaporated charged particles
 61ZN5c  were detected in the 40-element silicon |DE-E array ISIS. A total of   
 61ZN6c  27 |g rays are assigned in a level scheme up to 31/2. The level scheme 
 61ZN7c  is in agreement with that from 2006An31                                
 61ZN c  1999Vi12: E=65 MeV. Measured E|g, |g|g, I|g(singles and |g|g), and     
 61ZN2c  |g|g(|q)(DCO) using the AYEBALL array with TESSA type detectors,       
 61ZN3c  eight EUROGAM detectors and one GAMMASPHERE detector. A total of       
 61ZN4c  23 |g transitions were reported. There is disagreement in parity       
 61ZN5c  assignment for bands based on 124 level, as compared to                
 61ZN6c  results in 2006An31 and 2004Iz01. Also 1403-keV |g is a doublet,       
 61ZN7c  whereas only a single line is shown in 1999Vi12                        
 61ZN cG $R{-DCO}=[(I(158|') gated at I(79|',101|',134|'))/(                    
 61ZN2cG I(79|',101|',134|') gated at I(158|'))]x |e, where I is the number of  
 61ZN3cG counts in a peak and |e is an efficiency multiplication factor         
 61ZN4cG (1999Vi12).                                                            
 61ZN cG $R{-DCO}=I(|g{-1} at 156|'; gated with |g{-2} at 77|',103|')/I(|g{-1}  
 61ZN2cG at 77|',103|'; gated with |g{-2} at 156|' ), CLOVER detectors at 77|'  
 61ZN3cG and 103|' are equivalent as far as DCO ratios are concerned. Known     
 61ZN4cG stretched E2 transitions were used for gating, such the R{-DCO}=1.0    
 61ZN5cG is expected for stretched quadrupole transitions and R{-DCO}|?0.6 for  
 61ZN6cG stretched dipoles, |DJ=0 transitions have values                       
 61ZN7cG similar to stretched quadrupole transitions (2004Iz01).                
 61ZN cG $POL=[aN(perpendicular)-N(parallel)]/[aN(perpendicular)+N(parallel)],  
 61ZN2cG where a(E|g)=normalization function determined from the {+152}Eu source
 61ZN3cG calibration. POL takes positive values for pure stretched electrical   
 61ZN4cG radiation and negative values for pure stretched magnetic radiation    
 61ZN5cG (2004Iz01).                                                            
 61ZN cG $R{-154|',96|'}=Yield at 154|'/Yield at 96|'. Typical values are       
 61ZN2cG 1.6-1.7 for |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions and 0.7-0.8 for |DJ=1,       
 61ZN3cG dipole transitions (2006An31).                                         
